---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Page from "../components/Page.astro";

// This page is the URL printed on the back of every card, so its path must
// stay /print. Content mirrors docs/printing.md.
import manifest from "../data/cards.json";

// Filenames come from the generator (cheatcards.deck_sheets) so a renamed
// sheet cannot leave a dead link here; only the prose lives in the page.
type Sheet = (typeof manifest.sheets)[number];
const key = (s: Sheet) => [s.paper, s.mode, s.flip].filter(Boolean).join("-");

const LABEL: Record<string, { name: string; note: string }> = {
  "a4-fold": {
    name: "A4 — the whole set, one sheet",
    note: "Start here. Single-sided, fold, glue, cut. No duplex printer needed.",
  },
  "letter-fold": { name: "US Letter — the whole set", note: "Same, Letter paper." },
  "a4-duplex-long": {
    name: "A4 two-sided, flip on LONG edge",
    note: "Two complete sets per sheet. Pick the file that matches your printer setting.",
  },
  "a4-duplex-short": {
    name: "A4 two-sided, flip on SHORT edge",
    note: "Same sheet, laid out for the other flip.",
  },
  "letter-duplex-long": { name: "US Letter, LONG edge", note: "" },
  "letter-duplex-short": { name: "US Letter, SHORT edge", note: "" },
};

const sheet = (s: Sheet) => ({
  href: `/cards/${s.file}`,
  ...(LABEL[key(s)] ?? { name: s.file, note: "" }),
});

const DECK = manifest.sheets.filter((s) => s.mode === "fold").map(sheet);
const DUPLEX = manifest.sheets.filter((s) => s.mode === "duplex").map(sheet);

const VIEWERS = [
  [
    "Acrobat / Reader",
    "Page Sizing & Handling → Size → Actual size. Turn off “Auto portrait/landscape”.",
  ],
  [
    "macOS Preview",
    "Scale: 100 % radio button (not “Scale to Fit”). Pick A4 / US Letter, not the “borderless” variant.",
  ],
  ["Windows / Edge", "Page Sizing → Actual size."],
  [
    "Chrome",
    "More settings → Scale → Custom → 100. Its “Default” silently shrinks. Prefer another viewer.",
  ],
];
---

<Base
  title="Print the cards — Cubepath"
  description="Print the Cubepath card set at home: one fold-over sheet for all four cards, per-card reprints, and the settings that keep them wallet-sized."
>
  <Header active="print" />
  <Page>
    <h1>Print the cards</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Four cards: three numbered progression cards and one annex. Each one leaves you able to solve
      a cube, and each says on its own back what unlocks the next.
    </p>

    <section>
      <h2>1. Print the set</h2>
      <ul class="files">
        {
          DECK.map((f) => (
            <li>
              <a href={f.href}>{f.name}</a>
              <span>{f.note}</span>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
      <details>
        <summary>Two-sided instead? Pick the file that matches your flip setting.</summary>
        <ul class="files">
          {
            DUPLEX.map((f) => (
              <li>
                <a href={f.href}>{f.name}</a>
                <span>{f.note}</span>
              </li>
            ))
          }
        </ul>
        <p class="hint">
          There is deliberately no single file that works under either flip. The numeral on both
          faces is your check — cut one card first and make sure its front and back agree.
        </p>
      </details>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Or reprint one card</h2>
      <ul class="files">
        {
          manifest.cards.map((c) => (
            <li>
              <a href={c.route}>
                {c.num ? `${c.num}/${c.of}` : "A"} — {c.title}
              </a>
              <span>
                <a href={`/cards/${c.fold_pdf.a4}`}>A4</a> ·{" "}
                <a href={`/cards/${c.fold_pdf.letter}`}>Letter</a> ·{" "}
                <a href={`/cards/${c.card_pdf}`}>bare card</a> — four copies per sheet.
              </span>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>2. Print at 100 %</h2>
      <p>
        This is the one setting that matters. Never “Fit to page”, “Shrink oversized pages”, or
        “Scale to fit”. Each sheet carries an <strong>80 mm calibration bar</strong>{" "}
        in both margins — measure it after the first page. If it isn’t 80 mm, the scale is wrong and the
        card won’t fit a wallet slot.
      </p>
      <table>
        <tbody>
          {
            VIEWERS.map(([app, how]) => (
              <tr>
                <th>{app}</th>
                <td>{how}</td>
              </tr>
            ))
          }
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p class="hint">
        Check your printer driver’s own dialog too — a driver-level “Fit to Paper Size” overrides
        whatever the application asked for.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>3. Folding and two-sided</h2>
      <p>
        The default files are <strong>single-sided</strong>: print, crease the grey line, fold so
        both printed faces are outward, glue, then cut both layers together. That removes duplex
        registration error entirely, and works on printers with no duplex unit at all.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you do want two-sided, the set ships one file per flip direction. Each card carries its
        number on <em>both</em> faces, so a wrong flip is caught after cutting one card instead of after
        wasting the sheet.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>4. Paper and finishing</h2>
      <p>
        160–200 gsm feeds through most home printers. Cut on the grey hairlines — they run the full
        sheet, so one straight cut serves four cards.
      </p>
      <p class="hint">
        A standard 54 × 86 mm “credit card” laminating pouch leaves about 0.4 mm of total clearance
        and will not seal. Either keep it wallet-sized and don’t laminate (the folded 200 gsm card
        is stiff enough), or use a 60 × 90 mm business-card pouch and accept that the result no
        longer fits a wallet slot.
      </p>
    </section>

    <p class="lead">
      Also on paper: <a href="/cubepath.pdf">the full PDF guide</a>.
    </p>
  </Page>
</Base>

<style>
  /*
   * Layout only. Width, centring and gutter come from <Page>; .lead and .hint
   * come from tokens.css. A page that restates their colour or type is how the
   * site ended up with five content widths and two spellings of "soft aside".
   */
  section {
    margin-top: var(--space-5);
  }
  h2 {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }
  /* `p.hint` is spelled out because .hint is `margin: 0` — a caption default
     that would otherwise win over the element rule and jam the aside against
     the block above it. */
  p,
  p.hint {
    margin: var(--space-2) 0;
  }
  .files {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .files li {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-1) var(--space-3);
    align-items: baseline;
    padding: var(--space-3) 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .files a {
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .files span {
    color: var(--soft);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }
  table {
    border-collapse: collapse;
    width: 100%;
    margin: var(--space-3) 0;
  }
  th,
  td {
    text-align: left;
    vertical-align: top;
    padding: var(--space-2) var(--space-3) var(--space-2) 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }
  th {
    white-space: nowrap;
    color: var(--soft);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
</style>
